description:
Implement a reset synchronizer that generates a reset signal for a DDR SDRAM interface. The module employs a shift register with a depth defined by the parameter PIPE_DEPTH, which is utilized to introduce a delayed reset output in response to a clock signal. When the pre_clear signal is low, the shift register is reset to zero. Once pre_clear is high, the register shifts its values on each rising edge of the clock, initializing the first bit to high and propagating the previous values through the pipeline, ultimately producing a synchronized reset output from the last register bit. This design effectively ensures that the reset signal is asserted de-bounced and delayed, suitable for reliable operation in memory interfaces.
